\ upcase.ga - convert console input to upper case using two nodes
\
\ Node 000 passes each byte of input to node 001, which converts lower case
\ letters to upper case and sends the result back to be output.
\
\ Port names alternate across the chip so that neighbours use the same name
\ for the port between them: both nodes reach each other through right.

node 000
: main
    right a!  up b!        \ A addresses node 001, B the console
    begin @b ! @ !b again

node 001
: main
    right b!
    begin @b upcase !b again

\ -if jumps to then unless T is negative, without dropping T
: upcase ( c - C )
    dup -97 + -if drop ; then      \ below a
    -26 + -if drop -32 + ; then    \ a to z
    drop ;
